      "type": "explanation",
      "title": "Nested Loops",
      "content": "A nested loop is a loop inside a loop. The inner loop runs ALL its iterations for EACH iteration of the outer loop. If the outer loop runs 3 times and the inner loop runs 4 times, the inner code runs 3 × 4 = 12 times total!",
      "code": "for row in range(1, 4):\n    for col in range(1, 3):\n        print(row, col)",
      "highlights": [
        { "lines": [1], "note": "Outer loop: row goes 1, 2, 3." },
        { "lines": [2], "note": "Inner loop: for EACH row, col goes 1, 2. The inner loop completely restarts each time the outer loop advances." },
        { "lines": [3], "note": "Runs 3 × 2 = 6 times total." }
      ]
    },
